# 1️⃣ Multivalued Dependency (MVD)

## First Understand the Problem

Suppose we have:

| Student | Skill  | Hobby   |
| ------- | ------ | ------- |
| Akshay  | Python | Cricket |
| Akshay  | Python | Music   |
| Akshay  | SQL    | Cricket |
| Akshay  | SQL    | Music   |

---

## What's Happening?

Akshay has:

Skills:

```text id="s0v0a4"
Python
SQL
```

Hobbies:

```text id="t0w3zb"
Cricket
Music
```

---

Database creates every combination.

Result:

```text id="khgkvj"
Python + Cricket
Python + Music
SQL + Cricket
SQL + Music
```

Lots of repetition ❌

---

# Mental Model 🧠

Student has:

```text id="4wq1r3"
Many Skills
AND
Many Hobbies
```

These are independent.

But database mixes them together.

---

# What is MVD?

When:

```text id="69jmcy"
One attribute determines
multiple independent values
```

We write:

```text id="7n6y7x"
Student ↠ Skill
```

and

```text id="2wq9qx"
Student ↠ Hobby
```

Notice:

```text id="s3npxk"
↠
```

(Double arrow)

Used for MVD.

---

# Solution

Split tables.

---

## Student Skills

| Student | Skill  |
| ------- | ------ |
| Akshay  | Python |
| Akshay  | SQL    |

---

## Student Hobbies

| Student | Hobby   |
| ------- | ------- |
| Akshay  | Cricket |
| Akshay  | Music   |

---

Redundancy removed ✅

---

# Memory Trick 🧠

```text id="9avmh2"
MVD =
One thing
has multiple independent lists
```

---

# 2️⃣ Fourth Normal Form (4NF)

## Simple Rule

A table is in 4NF if:

```text id="f5sru0"
No non-trivial
multivalued dependencies
```

---

Don't memorize.

Remember:

```text id="scbwrm"
4NF removes MVD problems
```

---

# Mental Model

```text id="3m6u0w"
3NF removes dependency problems

4NF removes MVD problems
```

---

# Example

Bad:

| Student | Skill | Hobby |
| ------- | ----- | ----- |

Good:

Separate tables.

Now table becomes 4NF.

---

# Memory Trick

```text id="wy3hz7"
4NF = No independent multi-lists
```

---

# 3️⃣ Fifth Normal Form (5NF)

Very advanced.

Rarely used in placements.

---

## Why 5NF Exists?

Sometimes even after 4NF:

```text id="f3p14m"
Data can still be reconstructed incorrectly
```

from multiple joins.

5NF removes this issue.

---

# Simple Definition

```text id="nyq8ae"
5NF eliminates
join dependency problems
```

---

# Mental Model 🧠

Imagine:

You split data into many tables.

Later:

```text id="6dmg8l"
Joining them creates
incorrect combinations
```

5NF prevents that.

---

# Placement Advice 🎯

For most interviews:

Understanding:

```text id="0p4w5n"
1NF
2NF
3NF
BCNF
```

is usually enough.

Know:

```text id="3g8dvc"
4NF → MVD

5NF → Join Dependency
```

and you're already ahead of most students.

---

# Easy Ladder of Normalization

```text id="ibisr7"
1NF
↓
Atomic values

2NF
↓
No partial dependency

3NF
↓
No transitive dependency

BCNF
↓
Every determinant is candidate key

4NF
↓
No multivalued dependency

5NF
↓
No join dependency
```

---

# Python Connection 🧠

Bad structure:

```python
student = {
    "skills": ["Python", "SQL"],
    "hobbies": ["Cricket", "Music"]
}
```

If stored incorrectly, database creates all combinations.

4NF says:

```text id="gm5s4q"
Store skills separately

Store hobbies separately
```

